l muscles and  roar punched up at the seams like a  football player if you kind of like a  hunky mass of metal and gears under your  foot this one is the car for you the 911  is eminently recognizable yet after all  these years it's still impressive the  front end is flirtatious the rear is  muscle East and the headlights are  friendly  [Music]  there is plenty to see inside the Jaguar  lots of loud blue stitching performance  seats and even a handle for the front  passenger to hold on to for dear life  this is the least well done of our three  when it comes to interior quality and  design but it's still pretty great  Porsche was the first sporting brand to  introduce the PDK paddle shift  technology which is quicker and better  for city driving than the manual there  is also a back seat in this option  something the other two don't have now I  don't know please put anybody in that  back seat except for maybe your dog or  someone you don't like but it is back  there you can use it at pinch inside I  loved how the Mercedes look it has crazy  octopus-like round dials all the way  through the center and the dash and  everything felt thick and rich the  bottom line you can't go wrong with any  of these incredible machines but if you  want the whole package at the best value  the 911 is the clear winner  sure it's not as aggressive looking at  the AMG and it has less power than the  jack but it's incredible connection to  the ground  it's cozy perfect German handling its  superior suspension and it's minimal but  quality interior mean the 911 Carrera S  Cabriolet is more than stands its ground  [Music]  you

